  "details": "Udon is becoming more and more popular, and Udon-driven triggers are being used more and more often in the worlds, for optimization, automation, and game logic.\nHowever, these triggers can be a source of problems. It turns out that even if you don't use OnTriggerStay (or OnPlayerTriggerStay) anywhere, this event can cause a lot of lags. It is implemented in UdonBehaviour, so Unity tries to tell Udon every frame, for example, that some VRC_Pickup is present in some trigger for the mirror. Dozens of objects can intersect with dozens of trigger volumes, giving hundreds of OnTriggerStay per frame. The more dynamic objects there are in the world, the even more calls there are. In the worst case, the number of calls grows quadratically.\nIn my case, this is getting worse by the fact that I use UdonBehaviour on VRC_Pickup to track player activity and respawn items when they are \"forgotten\" - as a result, the number of OnTriggerStay doubles.\nAlso, OnTriggerStay is called from FixedUpdate, and FixedUpdate should not slow down otherwise there are problems with physics.\nIf desired, this problem can be solved by world creator redo Udon scripts in different ways, but this is not obvious and inattentive creators can lag the world without deep understanding.\nIt is difficult for me to say how to solve this problem on VRChat side. A similar problem was with Update and FixedUpdate in earlier versions of Udon, but then it was refined with the use of ManagedUpdate.\nIt seems there is no way to drop OnTriggerStay in UdonBehaviour, but may be it's possible to make some optimizations. For example, add _hasStayEvent (as well as _hasUpdateEvent) and try to return from OnTriggerStay as soon as possible without calling GetPlayerByGameObject (which uses slow GetComponent?) or avoid dict _eventTable (in RunEvent).\nMay belike LazyUdonBehaviour can be made, which will not implement every-frame methods at all, but only handlers of \"rare\" user event logic. In most cases, every-frame logic is rarely needed at all, so this version of UdonBehaviour can give a good optimization.",
